{
	"_doc": [
		"Shared schedule vectors (spec 0002, section 4.1). Read by PHP (integration) and TS (player, admin JS); every vector must have a result in each layer that reads it.",
		"Results are those of 3.4.2 until a spec fixes them (resolution: C16, K8 and K52, spec 0009). A vector whose result differs from the correct one has \"currently\": true, the docs/known-issues.md row in \"issue\" and the correct result in \"correct\".",
		"Days are schedule keys (monday ... sunday). Times are station-local HH:MM. Program keys refer to \"programs\": each test creates one published program per key, named after it; a key missing from \"programs\" stands for a program that does not exist.",
		"unpublished (resolution, optional): program keys that are not public in that vector (draft; ADR 0045). Each layer leaves them out of its programs map (or creates them as drafts).",
		"resolution: \"grid\" names an entry of \"grids\". current/upcoming.day is the day the slot belongs to; current.from is today or yesterday (a slot crossing midnight). upcoming.minutes is minutes until start. A vector where the player (TS) differs from PHP has a \"ts\" object with the player's current/upcoming, \"currently\": true and the issue; its top-level result is then the PHP one, and the correct one.",
		"tz: instant in UTC plus timezoneOffset (hours) gives the station-local day (0 = Sunday) and minutes since midnight.",
		"validation: \"php\" is radplapag_sanitize_station_schedule(), \"admin\" is admin/js/station-admin.js. error is the code of the first error reported (days Monday to Sunday, rows in order): required, invalid_program, format, overlap (same day), cross_midnight_overlap (slot crossing into the next day), start_equals_end (admin only). For admin it is the message the first row with an error shows after submit (another row's check can replace it), and slots are typed into <input type=\"time\">, which empties a value that is not a time (24:00).",
		"model: the week-interval model (ADR 0044) that PHP (Schedule\\Week_Interval), the player (utils/week-interval.ts) and the admin (radplapagScheduleRules) share. A minute of the week is day × 1440 + minute, Monday = 0 (0 ≤ w < 10080). from_slot gives a slot's { start, duration }; contains, minutes_until_start and overlaps take slots as { day, start, end } and instants as { day, time }. Results are the correct ones, the same in every layer."
	],
